sn35.136:4.1 starts: The stopping of self-identity
sn35.136:4.2 starts: is viewed by the noble ones
sn35.136:4.3 starts: This, when seen,
sn35.136:4.4 starts: runs counter
sn35.229:3.1 starts: Whoever has become dispassionate
sn35.229:3.2 starts: to passion, aversion, & ignorance,
sn35.229:3.3 starts: crosses over this ocean,
sn35.229:3.4 starts: waves,
sn35.240:3.1 starts: Like a turtle with its limbs withdrawn
sn35.240:3.2 starts: so the monk, the thoughts of the
sn35.240:3.3 starts: Not dependent, harming no others,
sn35.240:3.4 starts: totally unbound, he would berate no one.
